As we have seen, conductivity arises from mobile charge carriers. In metals,
            these mobile charge carriers are electrons; in an ionised gas, they are electrons and positive charged ions;
            in an electrolyte, these can be both positive and negative ions.

15. The potentiometer is a device to compare potential differences. Since the
            method involves a condition of no current flow, the device can be used to measure potential difference;
            internal resistance of a cell and compare emf’s of two sources.
